# DEFECT 2558, beside it: a null read the library before the runtime declines
# is still told (2026-11-15).
#
# The guard now asks the handler installed before it about a fault at a low
# address on a stack the runtime did not measure, and that handler may give
# the fault back: Go's archive, for a fault it did not make, puts SIGSEGV back
# to the default it found and returns, so the access would fault again and
# the process die at 139 in silence. The guard reads the register file before
# and after the call, finds it as it was, and tells the read as it always did.
# Under `--sanitize` the library hands the fault to the handler it found,
# AddressSanitizer's, which reports it (`fixedbugs-2558-library.h`).

extern "fixedbugs-2558-library.h"
    function lib_read_declined() -> i64

function main()
    print("before")
    print(lib_read_declined())
